# member_const_visibility_leak_rejected.tkr — a NAMESPACE-IDENTITY project-regressor (0.3.1
# regressor-principal, §5 triage exception): a `private` member const's visibility is gated by
# its DECLARING namespace, not an inheriting subclass's namespace. This can only be proven with
# a REAL cross-module project (a root-namespace `Base` + a `sub`-namespace `Sub` subclass) —
# flattening into one inline snippet would collapse the two namespaces into one and make the
# assertion vacuous (there would be no namespace boundary left to violate). Kept on disk,
# unflattened; not inline-scenario-izable.

Feature: member_const_visibility_leak_rejected — private member const does not leak across an inheriting subclass's namespace

  Scenario: a subclass's own namespace may not read a private const inherited from its base's namespace
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "member const `SECRET` is private to `Base`"
